# Get Medieval (KCD), 136 min of real streamed gameplay, b:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) 2026-10-08, build b043b35 (phase-step lookahead with late moves and the refusal); cut to the stretch the stream's video shows less its closing pause menu, 52.1 s to 8239.0 s
# units: microseconds. first value absolute, rest are deltas.
description Get Medieval (KCD), 136 min of real streamed gameplay, b:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) 2026-10-08, build b043b35 (phase-step lookahead with late moves and the refusal); cut to the stretch the stream's video shows less its closing pause menu, 52.1 s to 8239.0 s
# What the RELAY did on this capture. The replay model is only trustworthy
# for a configuration where it reproduces these; the test checks that.
field_worst_run 35
field_long_runs 0
field_synth_pct 0.3
field_pull_wraps 62
#
# WHAT IT COVERS: a whole stream, the longest of these at 136 minutes, cut to what its video
# shows, on the phase-step lookahead with late moves and the refusal. It is the first capture on
# the build that grabs at full size when the displays match and skips the ring copy of frames
# keep-real drops; neither touches the policy. The game hitched 131 times an hour and stalled for
# 100 ms or more 23 times an hour. Half the lookahead moves, 35 of 72, fall in the first 16
# minutes, up to 1000 s, 21 of them from 540 s to 700 s, where a dice game hitches once every
# 4.3 s (18 hitches from 562.6 s to 667.5 s, no stall). All 7 lock releases come while walking
# through one hall indoors, each 0.2 to 0.3 s after a hitch of 29 to 32 ms with no stall near:
# six from 1507.6 s to 2044.7 s and one at 6350.6 s. The worst blend run, 35 presents from
# 1507.5 s, runs through the first of them: a step is cancelled as it starts, the lock releases
# three presents in, and a late step comes as it ends. A second dice game, about 4880 s to
# 5480 s, has no hitch and no move; the game did not hitch at all from 2209 s to 4255 s or from
# 4347 s to 5558 s. The busiest stretch is a fight at night, 7185 s to 7403 s: 62 hitches and 18
# stalls of up to 311 ms, and 7 moves. 10 of the 72 moves land more than 2 ms from a real frame
# on the replay, 8 of them before 1250 s and 2 in the fight.
#
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 52.076 s, from the 2229 marked
# frames in its first 38 s. 1987 of them sit within 0.4 ms of that offset (p90); the other 242
# show their present a refresh or more late, in runs that open with a repeated frame on the
# capture side and close with a skipped one. The video runs 8193.1 s with no holes. Its first
# frame is gameplay; its last seconds show the game's pause menu, so the cut ends at 8239.0 s, 6 s
# before the video does. The game was in its 60 fps regime from 9 s to 8251 s. Every second inside
# the cut that falls out of the regime is a hitch second, 24 of them in 23 runs, none longer than
# 2 s, so nothing was removed from the middle.
#
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships, so the two lines are comparable. The
# replay reads synth 0.4% against 0.3% (0.3% on the dejitter arm, which is how the stream ran),
# worst run 35 against 35 at the same present, runs >= 50 0 against 0 and pull wraps 66 against
# 62. Counted over this window, blends are 1554 against 1551, repeats 440 against 441, skips 146
# against 146, lock releases 8 against 7 and lookahead moves 72 against 72: 58 steps seen, 1
# cancelled, 15 late and 4 refused in both. The 7 field releases are at the same presents in the
# replay, and 69 moves land on the same presents. At 160.4 s and 473.3 s both sides moved the
# same way two presents apart; the replay's move at 473.3 s landed 3.3 ms from a real frame and
# its lock released 4 presents later, the release the field does not have. At 7306.5 s the field
# stepped +4.7 ms, and the replay stepped -4.1 ms 26 presents later. Of the field's 62 pull
# wraps, 54 are in the replay within 50 ms and 7 more in the same direction up to 6 s apart; the
# one at 489.9 s is not. The replay adds two round trips, down and back up within 0.3 s, at
# 6424.8 s and 7556.6 s, and one wrap at 7306.6 s, between the field's step there and its own.
#
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran.
max_worst_run 35
max_long_runs 0
max_synth_pct 0.8
min_reseeds 82
max_pull_wraps 66
extra_lag_ms 75
